# gemma4-26b-a4b-df-i8.recipe -- Gemma 4 26B-A4B with the DFlash drafter: the routed experts'
# gate_up and the drafter at eight bits, and nothing in E4M3.
#
#   rad-convert <gemma-4-26B-A4B-it> --draft-model <gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-DFlash> \
#       --recipe data/recipes/gemma4-26b-a4b-df-i8.recipe -o gemma4-26b-a4b-dflash-i8.rad
#
#   - Every routed expert's gate/up projection as rotated int8: codes in -127..127 with a bf16
#     scale per (row, 128 of K), each 128 of K rotated by the unnormalised Hadamard
#     (`transform=fwht128`), round to nearest with a scale search. The grouped GEMM reads them at
#     i8a8h against int8 codes of the experts' input that the rotating norm writes
#     (rmsnorm_had_quant_i8g, moe_gemm_i8a8). They are nine tenths of the weight bytes.
#   - The experts' down projection stays bf16: its K is the
#     expert's 704 columns, which whole 128-column scale groups do not tile.
#   - The drafter's seven linears and its copy of the tied head on the int8 grid its block serves
#     (arch/common/rad_gemma4_dflash.h): int8 codes with an f16 scale per (row, 128 columns),
#     read at w8a8 against an int8 activation with a scale a row.
#
# The trunk's attention and dense arm, the norms, the router and the embedding stay bf16.

blk.*.ffn_gate_up_exps.*.weight      rtn codes=i8 group=128 scale=bf16 transform=fwht128 clamp=sym rule=search
dflash.fc.weight                     rtn codes=i8 group=128 scale=f16 clamp=sym
dflash.blk.*.attn_q.weight           rtn codes=i8 group=128 scale=f16 clamp=sym
dflash.blk.*.attn_k.weight           rtn codes=i8 group=128 scale=f16 clamp=sym
dflash.blk.*.attn_v.weight           rtn codes=i8 group=128 scale=f16 clamp=sym
dflash.blk.*.attn_output.weight      rtn codes=i8 group=128 scale=f16 clamp=sym
dflash.blk.*.ffn_gate_up.weight      rtn codes=i8 group=128 scale=f16 clamp=sym
dflash.blk.*.ffn_down.weight         rtn codes=i8 group=128 scale=f16 clamp=sym
dflash.draft_head.weight             rtn codes=i8 group=128 scale=f16 clamp=sym
